  "title": "Promise.all vs await-in-loop",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Three waits, two stories\n\n`await Player.wait(1)` three times in a row is **sequence**. `Promise.all([Player.wait(1), Player.wait(1), Player.wait(1)])` starts them together.\n\nThe fox still only moves after you say so. Use `wait` then walk east to (3, 0). Sequence is fine here — the lesson is that `all` would overlap the pauses."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "all-overlap",
      "promptMd": "`Promise.all` of three waits…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "sum",
          "md": "Always adds the times"
        },
        {
          "id": "max",
          "md": "Finishes when the slowest finishes (they overlap)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "max"
    },
